WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.800
It's one of the main priorities decided by
the EU leaders when they fixed the directions

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:11.800
for the next five years: build a European
Energy Union. It's crucial for the economy,

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.400
for Europe's security, and to fight climate
change.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.700
An effective energy Union can fundamentally
improve the situation in Europe - by ensuring

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:28.280
cheap, sustainable and secure energy for all:
states, companies, and citizens.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.420
The conflict between Russia and Ukraine, and
a row over gas prices, highlights the urgency

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:38.629
for the EU to increase its energy security.

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:45.629
More than half of our energy consumption is
imported. This costs a billion a day.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:52.760
This means that we have to take measures, specially
in the current geopolitical context, to, first

00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:59.199
of all, solve some of the problems in our
infrastructure, but also to reduce our external

00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:04.370
dependence, specially for those countries
who are dependent on a single supplier.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:10.640
The EU depends more and more on gas from external
suppliers. When gas is imported from different

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:16.560
sources and contracts are flexible, things
are fine, says European Council President Donald Tusk.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.860
But most bilateral contracts with Europe's
dominant supplier Russia, are concluded on

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:27.860
a long-term basis, sometimes more than 20
years, and that can be unhealthy, Tusk says.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:34.560
The EU's gas market was discussed by EU leaders
at their Spring summit in March.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:40.170
All leaders agreed to reinforce transparency
in the gas market, so suppliers cannot abuse

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:45.170
their position to break EU law and reduce
our energy security.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:51.050
Pooling energy resources across the EU is
another way to ensure energy security. But

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:56.050
in order to achieve this, renovation and better
interconnections of electricity grids and

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:03.050
gas pipelines are needed. So that energy surpluses
in one member state can be easily channelled

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.250
to another member state with a shortage.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:10.420
Here, Europe has gone forward. Not only have
we improved the connections between member

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:17.840
states, but we also supported Ukraine with
reverse-flow. This shows we were right in

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:24.700
our view that all states should be reachable
through gas pipelines.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:31.270
Recently, leaders of France, Spain and Portugal
agreed in Madrid to double the electricity

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:36.250
interconnection capacity between their three
countries, and to start a major gas project.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:43.250
Our common European project is to unite, integrate
and connect. We already removed artificial

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:50.440
borders between us and we shall now remove
natural ones.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:57.120
Meanwhile, in the EU's northern corner, Lithuania
opened its own LNG floating terminal in late

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:04.120
2014, labelled "Independence". With this terminal,
the Baltic state not only reduces its previously

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:10.370
100% dependency on Russia, but it can also
supply its neighbours.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:15.860
Achieving 10% interconnection is the goal
proposed by the European Commission in its

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:19.819
Energy Union plan. It will require serious
investment.

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:27.359
It is estimated that in the next two decades
we will need 200 billions a year to upgrade

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:35.210
our current systems, not only to meet future demand
but simply also to replace the existing infrastructure.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:42.489
What we need to do is give a direction to
that so that member states, market players,

00:03:42.489 --> 00:03:45.230
make the right investments.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:50.819
Investments which in turn will not only generate
economic growth and more jobs in the energy

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:57.239
sector, but also make energy cheaper. This
is crucial for Europe's competitiveness at a

00:03:57.239 --> 00:04:04.129
time when energy bills are 30% more expensive
in Europe than in the United States.

00:04:04.129 --> 00:04:10.040
Cleaner energy is a very important dimension
of Europe's Energy Union plan. The UN Climate

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:13.840
Change conference which will take place in
Paris this year provides a clear momentum

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:20.840
for a big push for more energy efficiency
and a new generation of renewables. The EU

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:26.440
is at the forefront of the decarbonisation
effort, and it wants other countries to follow.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:38.060
I thank Europe for being first in delivering
its climate pledge for the Paris Conference."

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:45.090
With a target of 40% cut in greenhouse gas
emissions by 2030, the EU leads the world's

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:53.830
fight against climate change. The Energy Union
is the main driving force to reach that target.

